{"id":"workloads-pods-scheduling-group","corpus":"k8s","title":"Scheduling Group","sourceUrl":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/scheduling-group/","license":"Kubernetes Documentation © The Kubernetes Authors, licensed CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Scheduling Group"},{"kind":"p","text":"More information about this feature"},{"kind":"p","text":"To use this feature, you (or a cluster administrator) will need to enable the GenericWorkload feature gate for all relevant components in your cluster."},{"kind":"p","text":"See Enable Or Disable Feature Gates for more information."},{"kind":"p","text":"You can link a Pod to a PodGroup to indicate that the Pod belongs to a group of Pods scheduled together. This enables the scheduler to apply group-level policies such as gang scheduling rather than treating each Pod independently."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Specifying a scheduling group"},{"kind":"p","text":"When the GenericWorkload feature gate is enabled, you can set the spec.schedulingGroup field in your Pod manifest. This field establishes a link to a specific PodGroup object in the same namespace by name."},{"kind":"p","text":"The schedulingGroup field is immutable. Once set, a Pod cannot be moved to a different PodGroup."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Behavior"},{"kind":"p","text":"When you set spec.schedulingGroup, the scheduler looks up the referenced PodGroup and applies the scheduling policy defined in it:"},{"kind":"li","text":"If the PodGroup uses the basic policy, each Pod is scheduled independently using standard Kubernetes behavior. The grouping is used as group-level label."},{"kind":"li","text":"If the PodGroup uses the gang policy, the Pod enters an \"all-or-nothing\" scheduling lifecycle. The scheduler tries to place at least minCount Pods in the group simultaneously; none of them bind to nodes unless the minimum is met."},{"kind":"p","text":"More information about this feature"},{"kind":"p","text":"To use this feature, you (or a cluster administrator) will need to enable the CompositePodGroup feature gate for all relevant components in your cluster."},{"kind":"p","text":"See Enable Or Disable Feature Gates for more information."},{"kind":"p","text":"When the CompositePodGroup feature gate is enabled, a PodGroup may also specify a parent CompositePodGroup. In a hierarchical workload, scheduling is governed by policies defined across the entire group tree (such as multi-level gang scheduling or topology constraints)."},{"kind":"h2","text":"Missing group references"},{"kind":"p","text":"If a Pod references a PodGroup that does not yet exist, the Pod remains pending. Similarly, if the referenced PodGroup specifies a parent CompositePodGroup (via spec.parentCompositePodGroupName) that has not been created yet, scheduling does not start and the Pod remains pending until the entire group hierarchy exists in the cluster."},{"kind":"p","text":"The scheduler automatically reconsiders the Pod once all required PodGroup and CompositePodGroup resources exist."},{"kind":"h2","text":"What's next"},{"kind":"li","text":"Learn about the PodGroup API and its lifecycle."},{"kind":"li","text":"Read about the CompositePodGroup API."},{"kind":"li","text":"Read about PodGroup scheduling policies."},{"kind":"li","text":"Understand the gang scheduling algorithm."}],"lemmas":{"scheduling":["scheduling","schedule"],"schedulings":["scheduling","schedulings"],"schedules":["schedule","schedules"],"groups":["group","groups"],"grouped":["grouped","group"],"features":["feature","features"],"featuring":["featuring","feature"],"featured":["featured","feature"],"clusters":["cluster","clusters"],"clustering":["clustering","cluster"],"clustered":["clustered","cluster"],"administrators":["administrator","administrators"],"wills":["will","wills"],"willing":["willing","will"],"willed":["willed","will"],"would":["would","will"],"needs":["need","needs"],"needed":["needed","need"],"needi